    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d779">

                <pb facs="0831" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 C 353/223</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Japanese
                        Embassy</hi><anchor n="47" xml:id="d779-f1"/></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi></p>
                <p>The American Government is highly gratified at the prompt expression of regret of
                    the Imperial Japanese Government, communicated <pb facs="0832" n="734"
                        xml:id="pg734"/> through the Japanese Ambassador in Washington, in
                    connection with the physical assault upon an American Consul, Mr. Culver B.
                    Chamberlain, at Mukden, on January 3.</p>
                <p>The American Government is, however, of the view, in which it believes that the
                    Japanese Government will readily concur, that, toward ensuring respect for
                    personal and official rights, it is desirable that the perpetrators of such
                    unlawful and unwarranted acts be promptly and adequately punished. The American
                    Government therefore desires to bring to the attention of the Imperial Japanese
                    Government this phase of the matter, with the request that suitable action in
                    these premises be taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, [<date calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-06">January 6,
                            1932?</date>.]</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d779-f1" n="47" type="source" xml:id="d779-f1-content">
                <p>Handed to the Japanese Ambassador by the Secretary of State on January 6,
                    1932.</p>
            </note>
